        "mission_intent": "We need a comprehensive collection plan focused on China's rapidly advancing space capabilities, specifically targeting three lines of effort: (1) the PLA's ISR constellation architecture and satellite communications modernization, including any indicators of closing the gap with U.S. military space systems; (2) Beijing's crewed lunar program timeline and progress toward landing astronauts on the Moon by approximately 2030 and establishing a permanent lunar base by the mid-2030s; and (3) the growth trajectory of China's commercial space sector and its competitive positioning against U.S. and European firms. For the ISR and SATCOM line, leverage SIGINT and GEOINT assets to characterize new constellation deployments and sensor integration across multi-sensor architectures, with particular attention to global coverage milestones. For the lunar program, task OSINT and MASINT collection against launch facilities and deep-space tracking infrastructure, cross-cueing with liaison reporting from allied space agencies. For commercial space, OSINT and FININT should map investment flows, launch cadence, and technology transfer indicators. Beidou PNT capability evolution relative to GPS and Galileo should be tracked as a crosscutting indicator across all three lines. Coordinate nominations through the National HUMINT Requirements Tasking Center where applicable. Initial collection nominations are due to the requirements manager by close of business Friday, with a full production-ready assessment expected within 45 days. All reporting should be classification-appropriate for inclusion in the next quarterly space threat update briefing to senior policymakers.",
